.TH FRITZ-XML-2VCARD 1 2026-10-15 "fritz-xml-2vcard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fritz-xml-2vcard \- convert a FRITZ!Box phone book export to vCard files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fritz-xml-2vcard
.I phonebook.xml
.I output-directory
.br
.B fritz-xml-2vcard
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fritz-xml-2vcard
reads a phone book exported from an AVM FRITZ!Box in XML format and writes
one vCard (version 3.0, UTF\-8) per contact into
.IR output-directory .
.PP
Each file is named after the contact's name, with spaces, commas, colons,
slashes and backslashes replaced by underscores, and gets the extension
.BR .vcf .
Contacts that would get the same file name are numbered, for example
.B Doe__John.vcf
and
.BR Doe__John_2.vcf .
Existing files with the same name in
.I output-directory
are overwritten.
.PP
Names, phone numbers of the types home, work, mobile, fax_work and
untyped numbers, as well as email addresses are converted.
See
.I CONVERSION.md
in the package for the complete mapping.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I phonebook.xml
Path to the FRITZ!Box phone book XML export.
.TP
.I output-directory
Directory to write the vCard files to.
It must already exist.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All contacts were converted.
.TP
.B 1
The usage summary was requested, arguments are missing, the input file or
the output directory could not be found, or required modules are not
installed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert the phone book
.I phonebook.xml
into the directory
.IR vcards :
.PP
.RS
.nf
mkdir -p vcards
fritz-xml-2vcard phonebook.xml vcards
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
Unlike the Node.js API and the web version, the command line tool does not
add area or country codes to phone numbers.
.PP
A web version is available at
.UR https://blog.rillke.com/fritzXML2vcard/
.UE .
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/Rillke/fritzXML2vcard/issues
.UE .
